From 29d8ea3055fd5f2ace231b5bb29cc84957c214f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:38:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/25] cpu: NativeCPU, a CPU without a JIT for recompiled code
 (SSD_AOT_NATIVE=1)

With every guest function the app runs recompiled, the JIT only drove
threads into native code. NativeCPU keeps the registers in the native
context and calls the native function at pc until the guest returns to
the kernel's halt instruction (registered with aot_set_halt). Escapes
continue at resume points; imports call the HLE function or the native
export directly; guest code without native code is a logged error that
ends the thread.

The hooks of recompiled code now dispatch through AotOwner, implemented
by DynarmicCPU and NativeCPU; AotEscape/AotUnwind are shared. DynarmicCPU
also copies TPIDRURO back from native code, which kernel modules write.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
